  "notes": "Captured 2026-10-13. jbhifi.com.au is a client-rendered Shopify storefront: WebFetch returns only <head> metadata (titles, meta descriptions) for the homepage and /pages/* (no header, nav, footer or body), web.archive.org is blocked, /account/login, /pages/privacy-policy and support.jbhifi.com.au are robots-disallowed, and /pages/gift-cards, /pages/new, /pages/clearance, /collections/new, /collections/clearance, /collections/gift-cards and /collections/games-hardware returned client errors. What was fetched: the sitemap index and the pages/collections/blogs sitemaps (real handles such as /pages/store-finder, /pages/track-my-order, /pages/perks, /pages/installations, /pages/tradein, /pages/extracare, /pages/interest-free-finance, /pages/receipts, /pages/catalogues, /pages/brands, /pages/about-us, /blogs/news-and-reviews, /blogs/competitions, /collections/computers-tablets, /collections/mobile-phones, /collections/music), page titles (\"Order Tracking\", \"JB Hi-Fi Store Finder\", \"Current catalogues - Shop Red Hot Deals at JB Hi-Fi!\", \"Products\" H1 on /collections/all, \"About us - JB Hi-Fi\", \"Electronic Brands\") and the PDP body (Description, Availability, Returns policy and Warranty guide help links). Header utilities and the nine nav entries come from research/jb-hifi.md (live browser walk 2026-09-29). The footer column contents, the homepage section list, the department tree (based on the collections sitemap handles) and the help/policy copy are reconstructed from those URLs, the PDP help links and the research/jb-hifi.md help-article quotes; they could not be checked against a rendered footer or homepage. New, Clearance, Services and Gift Cards keep local paths because the real URL could not be confirmed. Off-site JB properties (careers.jbhifi.com.au, the investor site, JB Hi-Fi Business, JB Hi-Fi Education, corporate gift cards) are local summary pages. The real site has no HTML site map; the clone serves /sitemap and /sitemap.xml.",
